                        "entry_id": "3345c086-aa8b-329f-a063-32a23938c0d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A finale; something that is conclusively better, or \\\"caps it all off\\\"."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46c174f7-55d5-4ee1-9f28-9308bc47eba9",
                                "sense_id": "9557e66e-e17e-3c87-8023-b03fcc7dddfc",
                                "text": "And the capper of it all was, Stacy flew back to Memphis to see me for a day and try to settle our divorce with a one-on-one meeting."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b37875f-540d-44c1-8dee-459692c0d389",
                                "sense_id": "9557e66e-e17e-3c87-8023-b03fcc7dddfc",
                                "text": "The real capper is when St. John starts fawning over Hugh Hefner, host of the finest Super Bowl party known to man, musing: “The question isn’t whether Hef is the hippest octogenarian on the planet."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
